      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before the town, a 4,000‑acre Helena Plantation was gifted to John Ferriday in 1812, marking the area’s first European settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Ferriday,_Louisiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Delta Music Museum celebrates Ferriday’s musical heritage, honoring Jerry Lee Lewis, Mickey Gilley, and Jimmy Swaggart as hometown icons.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
